ite operations and `repositoryFullName` for uniqueness/provenance. `repositoryFullName` is derived server-side when omitted. | Resolved - clarified |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:36:| Refresh cannot always settle synchronously | AC-3.3, Refresh Response | Design returns `refreshStatus: settled | pending | failed`, with pending as operation metadata rather than a fifth hydration state. | Resolved - clarified |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:37:| Process-scoped shadowing needs exact read rule | Tech Design Question 7 | Design defines an active-source resolver that combines project-scoped and process-scoped attachments, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, and excludes detached rows. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:38:| Detach representation needs exact storage shape | Tech Design Question 8 | Design adds soft-detach fields (`detachedAt`, `detachedByUserId`) and active-list filters. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:39:| Source provenance storage is deferred by epic | AC-4.x | Design introduces durable `sourceProvenance` records with copied immutable source identity. | Resolved |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:42:continues to own source-management policy and orchestration; Convex owns durable\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:49:| 1 | What exact browser interaction model should attach, update, refresh, and detach use without creating a separate source-management app? | Extend the existing project shell and process work surface. Project-scoped actions appear in the project source section; process-scoped actions appear in the process materials/source area. Client calls Fastify JSON APIs and renders settled/pending/degraded responses in-place. No standalone source app or live source subscription is added. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:50:| 2 | What exact durable schema should represent source attachments and provenance visibility? | Extend `sourceAttachments` with `repositoryFullName`, freshness fields, refresh progress fields, and soft-detach fields. Add `sourceProvenance` for process-specific provenance with copied immutable source identity. Artifact ownership remains untouched. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:51:| 3 | What exact conflict rule applies for same repository/target ref across related contexts? | Duplicate key is active `projectId + processId + repositoryFullName + targetRef`. Same identity/ref may exist once at project scope and once at process scope. Process-scoped rows shadow project-scoped rows only for that process's current-source read. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:53:| 5 | What provenance surface shows informed-work and received-code-update relationships? | Add a process provenance endpoint and client section that reads durable `sourceProvenance` entries. Entries are `informed_work` or `received_code_update`, copy repository identity, and enrich current attachment context independently when available. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:55:| 7 | What exact current-source read algorithm combines scopes and degrades boundedly? | `resolveActiveProcessSources` excludes detached rows, starts from current material refs, pulls in process-scoped siblings when they shadow an active project-scoped source, partitions by scope, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, sorts by `updatedAt`, and preserves per-row degraded metadata. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:56:| 8 | What soft-detach representation preserves identity and provenance? | Add `detachedAt` and `detachedByUserId` to source attachments. Active listings filter detached rows, but provenance entries remain durable because they copy identity and may retain nullable `sourceAttachmentId`. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:61:already made source attachments visible enough for hydration and checkpointing,\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:63:`sourceAttachments` table, project shell summaries expose attached sources, and\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:79:provenance intent. Convex stores durable source attachment and provenance rows\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:85:those provenance records without asking source attachments to become archive\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:94:| Projects | Core architecture | Project-scoped source attachments appear in the project shell and can be managed there |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:97:| Environments | Core architecture | Hydrates active source attachments and reports freshness/checkpoint effects |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:138:| Convex | Durable source attachment and provenance persistence | Use Convex function tests for durable invariants; in Fastify service tests use existing PlatformStore fakes or in-memory harnesses |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:144:| WorkOS-authenticated Fastify request | All source-management routes | Existing au