eshness-management.md:33:- Initial source attachment\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:37:- Separate live source-management subscription\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:49:**AC-3.1:** Each source attachment shows whether it is not hydrated, hydrated, stale, or unavailable.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:52:  - Given: One or more source attachments exist\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:54:  - Then: Each source attachment shows its current hydration or freshness state\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:56:**AC-3.2:** If a source attachment is `stale` or `not_hydrated`, the platform shows a rehydration or refresh path. `Unavailable` attachments do not falsely promise recovery.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:59:  - Given: A source attachment is stale\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:60:  - When: The source attachment appears in the current surface\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:63:  - Given: A source attachment is unavailable and not currently recoverable\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:64:  - When: The source attachment appears in the current surface\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:67:  - Given: A source attachment is not yet hydrated\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:68:  - When: The source attachment appears in the current surface\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:71:**AC-3.3:** Rehydrating or refreshing one source attachment updates that source state without erasing the rest of the source-management surface.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:74:  - Given: User requests rehydration or refresh for one stale or not-yet-hydrated source attachment\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:76:  - Then: That source attachment updates in place without hiding the rest of the source list\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:78:  - Given: User requested refresh for one source attachment\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:80:  - Then: The current surface shows that refresh is in progress for that source attachment\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:104:| `refreshStatus` | enum | yes | `settled`, `pending`, or `failed` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md:113:- Recoverable missing working copy is represented as `stale` with `freshnessReason`, not as a fifth enum value.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-mana