ity/004-verify.json\"\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:14:- **Context:** The user is starting or resuming work inside a concrete project. They need one durable container that holds processes, artifacts, and source attachments before deeper process-specific behavior begins.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:29:- Project shell sections for processes, artifacts, and source attachments\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:53:**AC-3.1:** The project shell shows separate sections for processes, project artifacts, and source attachments, including clear empty states when a section has no items.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:56:  - Given: Project contains processes, artifacts, and source attachments\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:60:  - Given: Project has no processes, no artifacts, and no source attachments\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:64:  - Given: Project has processes but no artifacts or source attachments\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:117:**AC-3.4:** Each source attachment summary shows repository identity and high-level source state, including purpose, target ref when available, hydration or freshness status, and when needed whether the source is attached at project level or for a specific process.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:121:  - When: The source attachment appears in the shell\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:132:  - Given: The project contains multiple source attachments with different update times\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:133:  - When: The source attachment list renders\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:136:  - Given: A source attachment is tied to a specific process rather than only the project\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:147:  - Given: The project shell can load processes and artifacts but source attachment data fails to load\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:151:  - Given: The project shell can load project identity, artifacts, and source attachments but process summary data fails to load\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:164:In Epic 1, the project shell read path returns all process summaries needed to render and validate project-level process selection. The selected process is derived from the current browser route and matched against the returned `processes.items` collection. The shell read path may also return section-level error states for `processes`, `artifacts`, or `sourceAttachments` without failing the entire project-shell response when project identity and access still succeed. This story does not add a separate single-process read endpoint or a server-persisted selected-process write path.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:182:| sourceAttachments | Source Attachment Section Envelope | yes | present | Current source attachment summaries or section-level source load state |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/01--project-and-process-shell/stories/03-project-shell-summaries.md:259:| sourceAttachmentId | string | yes | non-empty | Stable source attachment identifier |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility/