nt/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md:149:- Render degraded entries with durable repository identity and target ref.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-150-- Keep healthy provenance entries visible when one entry degrades.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-151-\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-152-#### Implementation Targets\n--\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-173-| TC-4.1b | `tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts` | renders empty provenance state |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-174-| TC-4.2a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | returns receiving source provenance |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-175-| TC-4.3a | `tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts` | read-only source not recorded as write target |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md:176:| TC-4.4a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` | degraded provenance entry does not hide healthy entries |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md:177:| TC-4.4b | `tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts` | degraded provenance falls back to durable identity |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-178-\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-179-#### Non-TC Decided Tests\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-180-\n--\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-187-\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-188-#### Anti-Shim Requirements\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-189-\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md:190:- Prove degraded provenance through the actual API/read surface, not only by inspecting stored rows.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-191-\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-192-#### Verification\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-193-\n--\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-207-- Process source provenance endpoint returns `informed_work` and `received_code_update` entries\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-208-- Provenance entries copy immutable repository identity, URL, and target ref\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-209-- Read-only sources are never shown as durable code-write targets\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md:210:- Empty provenance and degraded provenance states are visible in the process surface\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md:211:- One degraded provenance relationship does not fail the whole provenance read\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/04-provenance-and-canonical-source-visibility.md-212-- Planned tests for TC-4.1a through TC-4.4b are implemented in the files mapped by the test plan\n--\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-46-\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-47-| # | Epic Question | Design Answer |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-48-|---|---------------|---------------|\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:49:| 1 | What exact browser interaction model should attach, update, refresh, and detach use without creating a separate source-management app? | Extend the existing project shell and process work surface. Project-scoped actions appear in the project source section; process-scoped actions appear in the process materials/source area. Client calls Fastify JSON APIs and renders settled/pending/degraded responses in-place. No standalone source app or live source subscription is added. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-50-| 2 | What exact durable schema should represent source attachments and provenance visibility? | Extend `sourceAttachments` with `repositoryFullName`, freshness fields, refresh progress fields, and soft-detach fields. Add `sourceProvenance` for process-specific provenance with copied immutable source identity. Artifact ownership remains untouched. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-51-| 3 | What exact conflict rule applies for same repository/target ref across related contexts? | Duplicate key is active `projectId + processId + repositoryFullName + targetRef`. Same identity/ref may exist once at project scope and once at process scope. Process-scoped rows shadow project-scoped rows only for that process's current-source read. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-52-| 4 | What exact refresh/freshness policy maps to the four source states? | The canonical states remain `not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, and `unavailable`. Target-ref changes make hydrated rows stale. Refresh returns settled/pending/failed operation metadata; pending is not a fifth hydration state. Branch freshness is checked when the surface reads or refresh is requested, not by background polling. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:53:| 5 | What provenance surface shows informed-work and received-code-update relationships? | Add a process provenance endpoint and client section that reads durable `sourceProvenance` entries. Entries are `informed_work` or `received_code_update`, copy repository identity, and enrich current attachment context independently when available. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-54-| 6 | How should shell/process surfaces stay coherent across project and process scope? | Keep project shell source summaries for project-wide management. Process work surfaces show current sources after active-source resolution, including process-scoped shadowing and applicable project-scoped rows. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:55:| 7 | What exact current-source read algorithm combines scopes and degrades boundedly? | `resolveActiveProcessSources` excludes detached rows, starts from current material refs, pulls in process-scoped siblings when they shadow an active project-scoped source, partitions by scope, shadows by `repositoryFullName + targetRef`, sorts by `updatedAt`, and preserves per-row degraded metadata. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-56-| 8 | What soft-detach representation preserves identity and provenance? | Add `detachedAt` and `detachedByUserId` to source attachments. Active listings filter detached rows, but provenance entries remain durable because they copy identity and may retain nullable `sourceAttachmentId`. |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-57-\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-58-## Context\n--\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-196-└── materials-section.reader.ts                  # MODIFIED: active-source resolver and process shadowing\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-197-\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-198-apps/platform/client/features/projects/\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:199:└── source-attachment-section.ts                 # MODIFIED: management controls and pending/degraded state display\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-200-\ndocs/spec-build/v