urable schema should represent source attachments and provenance visibility? | Extend `sourceAttachments` with `repositoryFullName`, freshness fields, refresh progress fields, and soft-detach fields. Add `sourceProvenance` for process-specific provenance with copied immutable source identity. Artifact ownership remains untouched. |\n51-| 3 | What exact conflict rule applies for same repository/target ref across related contexts? | Duplicate key is active `projectId + processId + repositoryFullName + targetRef`. Same identity/ref may exist once at project scope and once at process scope. Process-scoped rows shadow project-scoped rows only for that process's current-source read. |\n52:| 4 | What exact refresh/freshness policy maps to the four source states? | The canonical states remain `not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, and `unavailable`. Target-ref changes make hydrated rows stale. Refresh returns settled/pending/failed operation metadata; pending is not a fifth hydration state. Branch freshness is checked when the surface reads or refresh is requested, not by background polling. |\n53-| 5 | What provenance surface shows informed-work and received-code-update relationships? | Add a process provenance endpoint and client section that reads durable `sourceProvenance` entries. Entries are `informed_work` or `received_code_update`, copy repository identity, and enrich current attachment context independently when available. |\n54-| 6 | How should shell/process surfaces stay coherent across project and process scope? | Keep project shell source summaries for project-wide management. Process work surfaces show current sources after active-source resolution, including process-scoped shadowing and applicable project-scoped rows. |\n--\n68-The missing layer is user- and process-facing source management. A user needs to\n69-attach a GitHub repository to a project or to one process, classify why it is\n70:attached, understand whether it can receive writes, refresh stale or missing\n71-working copies, detach it from current use without erasing history, and later\n72-understand which sources informed or received process work. Those behaviors\n--\n76-sandboxed filesystem is only a disposable working copy. Fastify is the source\n77-management control plane: it validates repository identity, enforces project and\n78:process access, resolves shadowing rules, coordinates refresh, and records\n79-provenance intent. Convex stores durable source attachment and provenance rows\n80-behind Fastify with validators and indexes that preserve integrity.\n--\n145-| GitHub token/config | Repository validation and branch freshness checks | Epic 6 introduces a dedicated `GitHubRepositoryResolver` seam over the existing app GitHub configuration |\n146-| Convex deployment/local backend | Durable source and provenance records | `pnpm run convex:dev` for runtime; tests use in-memory/mocked stores |\n147:| Environment refresh seam | Refresh/recovery paths | Epic 6 introduces a dedicated source refresh seam over existing process/environment services rather than assuming a full source-management implementation already exists |\n148-| Existing verification scripts | Story execution | `pnpm run red-verify`, `pnpm run verify`, `pnpm run green-verify`, `pnpm run verify-all` |\n149-\n--\n180-\n181-apps/platform/server/routes/\n182:└── source-management.ts                         # NEW: Fastify routes for attach/update/refresh/detach/provenance\n183-\n184-apps/platform/server/services/sources/\n--\n186-├── source-identity.service.ts                   # NEW: URL parsing, canonical full-name derivation, target-ref normalization\n187-├── github-repository-resolver.ts                # NEW: GitHub access/ref validation boundary\n188:├── source-refresh.service.ts                    # NEW: refresh request handling and pending/settled result shaping\n189-└── source-provenance.service.ts                 # NEW: provenance record creation/read enrichment\n190-\n--\n220-| `registerSourceManagementRoutes` | New | Authenticated Fastify API entry points | SourceManagementService, access services | AC-1.x through AC-6.x |\n221-| `SourceManagementService` | New | Attach/update/detach orchestration, conflict rules, scope enforcement | PlatformStore, SourceIdentityService, GitHubRepositoryResolver | AC-1.x, AC-2.x, AC-5.x, AC-6.2 |\n222:| `SourceRefreshService` | New | Refresh request policy, settled/pending/failed response mapping | PlatformStore, environment/service hooks, GitHub resolver | AC-3.x |\n223-| `SourceProvenanceService` | New | Record/read provenance, enrich degraded entries independently | PlatformStore | AC-4.x, AC-5.2 |\n224-| `MaterialsSectionReader` | Modified | Resolve current process sources with process-scoped shadowing and detached filtering | PlatformStore | AC-2.1, AC-3.1, AC-6.1 |\n--\n249-  lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n250-  freshnessReason: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n251:  refreshStatus: v.union(v.literal('idle'), v.literal('pending'), v.literal('failed')),\n252:  refreshRequestedAt: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n253-  detachedAt: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n254-  detachedByUserId: v.union(v.string(), v.null()),\n--\n281-- `lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef`: the most recently observed remote branch resolution\n282-\n283:For branch refs, the read/refresh path resolves the current remote branch head\n284-and compares it to `lastHydratedResolvedRef`. If they differ, the source becomes\n285-`stale`. For tag or commit refs on `read_only` attachments, Epic 6 treats the\n--\n374-  lastObservedRemoteResolvedRef: string | null;\n375-  freshnessReason: string | null;\n376:  refreshStatus?: 'idle' | 'pending' | 'failed';\n377:  refreshRequestedAt?: string | null;\n378-  detachedAt?: string | null;\n379-  updatedAt: string;\n--\n382-export interface RefreshSourceAttachmentResponse {\n383-  sourceAttachment?: SourceAttachmentSummary;\n384:  refreshStatus: SourceRefreshStatus;\n385:  refreshRequestedAt?: string;\n386-}\n387-\n--\n411-| Attach process source | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-attachments` | `attachProcessSource` |\n412-| Update source | PATCH | `/api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments/:sourceAttachmentId` | `updateSource` |\n413:| Refresh source | POST | `/api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments/:sourceAttachmentId/refresh` | `refreshSource` |\n414-| Detach source | DELETE | `/api/projects/:projectId/source-attachments/:sourceAttachmentId` | `detachSource` |\n415-| Get process source provenance | GET | `/api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/source-provenance` | `listProcessSourceProvenance` |\n--\n482-}\n483-\n484:export interface SourceRefreshService {\n485:  refreshSource(args: {\n486-    actor: AuthenticatedActor;\n487-    projectId: string;\n--\n557-This flow covers AC-2.1 through AC-2.4. Purpose and access mode are durable\n558-metadata. Target ref is part of the source definition; changing it marks a\n559:previously hydrated attachment stale until refresh/rehydration catches up.\n560-\n561-`SourceManagementService.updateSource` validates the actor, loads the active\n--\n575-\n576-This flow covers AC-3.1 through AC-3.3. The four canonical states remain\n577:`not_hydrated`, `hydrated`, `stale`, and `unavailable`. Pending refresh is not a\n578:state in that enum; it is operation progress metadata returned by refresh and\n579-visible in the client.\n580-\n--\n590-  the ref becomes unavailable\n591-- for project-scoped sources surfaced on the project shell, only offer or accept\n592:  refresh when exactly one current process working-copy target can be resolved;\n593-  otherwise the project-shell control should be hidden/disabled and the backend\n594:  should return request-level refresh-not-available rather than inventing a\n595-  target\n596-\n--\n600-    participant C as Client Source UI\n601-    participant R as Fastify Source Route\n602:    participant F as SourceRefreshService\n603-    participant P as PlatformStore\n604-    participant E as Environment Service\n605-\n606:    U->>C: Click refresh\n607:    C->>R: POST /refresh\n608:    R->>F: refreshSource\n609-    F->>P: get source attachment\n610:    alt Cheap freshness check or rehydration completes\n611:        F->>E: refresh or validate working copy\n612-        F->>P: update hydration/freshness\n613:        F-->>R: refreshStatus settled + sourceAttachment\n614-    else Longer work needed\n615:        F->>P: mark refresh pending\n616:        F-->>R: refreshStatus pending\n617-    else Not recoverable\n618:        F-->>R: request-level error or refreshStatus failed\n619-    end\n620-    R-->>C: Visible settled/pending/failed state\n--\n721-| 1 | Attach repositories | Routes, service validation, GitHub resolver, duplicate checks, process current-source mutation | AC-1.x | Relevant sections: Flow 1, Service Interfaces, Error Codes. Non-TC: URL/full-name mismatch, writable-ref policy, non-GitHub rejection |\n722-| 2 | Manage metadata | Update route, target-ref stale logic, UI metadata display | AC-2.x | Relevant sections: Flow 2, API Contracts. Non-TC: none |\n723:| 3 | Hydration/freshness | Refresh route, pending/settled/failed responses, branch snapshot comparison, freshness UI | AC-3.x | Relevant sections: Flow 3, Data Model. Non-TC: branch-head drift, refresh contract semantics |\n724-| 4 | Provenance | Provenance records, process read endpoint, degraded enrichment, redaction behavior | AC-4.x | Relevant sections: Flow 4, Data Model, API Contracts. Non-TC: unavailable-source redaction |\n725-| 5 | Detach | Soft detach, active-list filtering, provenance retention | AC-5.x | Relevant sections: Flow 5, Active Source Resolution. Non-TC: detached-row durability |\n--\n751-| Decision | Applied In |\n752-|----------|------------|\n753:| Pending refresh is stored on the source row with `refreshStatus` and `refreshRequestedAt`; Epic 6 does not add a separate refresh-operations table. | Chunk 3 |\n754-| `read_write` attachments require branch-like target refs. `read_only` attachments may use branch, tag, or commit refs. | Chunk 1 |\n755:| Provenance is recorded only for execution-time source influence and durable code updates, never for manual refresh. | Chunk 4 |\n756-\n757-## Self-Review Checklist\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
