Hub API / clone identity | Validate repository existence, access, canonical `owner/name`, and target ref resolution | Mock in server service tests through a `GitHubRepositoryResolver` interface |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-137-| Environment provider | Refresh or rehydrate working copies when needed | Mock provider adapter/service in process-level tests; do not mock internal source services |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-138-| Convex | Durable source attachment and provenance persistence | Use Convex function tests for durable invariants; in Fastify service tests use existing PlatformStore fakes or in-memory harnesses |\n--\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-143-|--------------|--------------|---------------|\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-144-| WorkOS-authenticated Fastify request | All source-management routes | Existing auth middleware populates `request.actor` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:145:| GitHub token/config | Repository validation and branch freshness checks | Epic 6 introduces a dedicated `GitHubRepositoryResolver` seam over the existing app GitHub configuration |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-146-| Convex deployment/local backend | Durable source and provenance records | `pnpm run convex:dev` for runtime; tests use in-memory/mocked stores |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-147-| Environment refresh seam | Refresh/recovery paths | Epic 6 introduces a dedicated source refresh seam over existing process/environment services rather than assuming a full source-management implementation already exists |\n--\n